1
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:29,154
FROM ME TO YOU: KIMI NI TODOKE
3RD SEASON

2
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:24,000
CHRISTMAS PARTY

3
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:27,629
Oh, the Christmas thing?

4
00:01:27,712 --> 00:01:29,798
It's after the end-of-term
ceremony, right?

5
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:34,010
- You going?
- Totally! What you gonna wear?

6
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:37,680
I just got a really cute dress.

7
00:01:37,764 --> 00:01:39,891
You and Andy signing up too, Yui?

8
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:42,227
We're celebrating together,
but totally!

9
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:44,896
It says to bring a present!
Any ideas?

10
00:01:44,979 --> 00:01:46,856
Huh? What about you, Sadako?

11
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:49,067
Gonna go?

12
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:50,860
We're all signing up, right now.

13
00:01:50,944 --> 00:01:54,364
I... I think that I could go.

14
00:01:57,242 --> 00:01:59,536
I'm just so glad that
you're able to join us this year.

15
00:01:59,619 --> 00:02:02,580
- Yay!
- Last year, we all sang a song at karaoke!

16
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:07,085
Wah!
For some reason, I'm incredibly excited!

17
00:02:08,086 --> 00:02:10,463
Hey! Not so fast!

18
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:12,215
How did things end up like this?!

19
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:14,050
What exactly did I just witness?

20
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:18,012
We get to spend the holidays together
as a couple this year.

21
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:19,973
But it doesn't count if it's a party!

22
00:02:20,056 --> 00:02:23,059
I mean, we're talking about
a huge group of people, y'know.

23
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:26,563
I can't take my eyes off her
for over two minutes, I swear.

24
00:02:26,646 --> 00:02:27,856
And then there's Chizu...

25
00:02:29,399 --> 00:02:32,277
And you're okay with that,
Sawako? For real?

26
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:36,447
Well, for me, as long as I'm spending time
with Kazehaya, I'm happy.

27
00:02:37,031 --> 00:02:41,953
Besides, I thought that if I was also
with you guys and everyone else,

28
00:02:42,036 --> 00:02:44,455
there's no way that
it wouldn't be fun, you know?

29
00:02:44,539 --> 00:02:48,585
Oh, right, you couldn't make it
to the Christmas party last year, huh?

30
00:02:48,668 --> 00:02:49,502
Yeah.

31
00:02:51,129 --> 00:02:54,716
Well, either way,
I'm pretty sure Kazehaya's figured out

32
00:02:54,799 --> 00:02:56,384
what he's dealing with by now.

33
00:02:57,594 --> 00:03:00,972
Hey, man! Why aren't the two of you
spending Christmas together?

34
00:03:01,055 --> 00:03:03,766
I expect this from someone like Joe,
but not you.

35
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:06,603
- Wahoo! Wahoo! Wahoo! Wahoo!
- No, it's not.

36
00:03:06,686 --> 00:03:09,939
- It's nothing like that, okay?
- Hmm? Really?

37
00:03:12,525 --> 00:03:14,319
So it's for Sadako?

38
00:03:15,069 --> 00:03:16,696
Just drop it!

39
00:03:16,779 --> 00:03:21,409
You're in love! It's your first Christmas
since you two started dating each other.

40
00:03:21,492 --> 00:03:24,454
Y'know you really oughta
spend it together, makin' out and stuff.

41
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:28,374
- Dude, I can't! Just back off, okay!
- Mmm?

42
00:03:31,085 --> 00:03:32,212
Got it!

43
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:34,505
So it's for Kazehaya's sake as well.

44
00:03:35,089 --> 00:03:35,924
Mmm?

45
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:39,969
Uh...

46
00:03:41,095 --> 00:03:42,764
A Christmas party, huh?

47
00:03:42,847 --> 00:03:44,057
With karaoke?

48
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:46,017
Shame I can't make it, I sing great.

49
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:48,895
If you ask me, it's a good thing
no one invited you to come.

50
00:03:48,978 --> 00:03:50,396
And you better not show up.

51
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,940
You idiot!

52
00:03:52,023 --> 00:03:54,525
You understand what day
we're talkin' about, right?

53
00:03:54,609 --> 00:03:58,029
- It says Christmas Par--
- I'm a busy adult with lots of big plans.

54
00:03:58,112 --> 00:04:01,157
I ain't got time to hang out with kids,
you dumb brat!

55
00:04:01,824 --> 00:04:05,119
Got me a date with a nurse
at a group dating thing!

56
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:08,873
Yeah, I'm pretty convinced
that our teacher's an actual child.

57
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:12,252
- Anyway, you goin', or...
- Huh?

58
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:14,587
The hell?!

59
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:18,216
- Ha! Must suck to be so lonely!
- Well, I'm not. At all!

60
00:04:18,299 --> 00:04:20,551
Also, I never said
whether or not I was going!

61
00:04:21,135 --> 00:04:23,429
Huh? You should go
with what's his name over there.

62
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:24,639
Miura.

63
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:26,516
Huh?

64
00:04:26,599 --> 00:04:27,475
Kento?!

65
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:29,185
But why?

66
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:32,689
Mr. Pin, I'm sorry,
but could you please not joke about that?

67
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:37,193
It's just that...
I'm pretty serious about her, y'know?

68
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,490
Huh?! You shoulda said so!

69
00:04:42,573 --> 00:04:44,909
What are you guys
reenacting the Battle of Tennozan?

70
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:46,703
Way to put the pressure on, man!

71
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:48,913
Okay, but you need to
seriously cut it out.

72
00:04:48,997 --> 00:04:51,666
Ge... get the hell outta my way!

73
00:04:51,749 --> 00:04:54,043
Two big idiots just make one big obstacle!

74
00:04:55,044 --> 00:04:56,754
Where are you goin'? Piss time?

75
00:04:56,838 --> 00:04:58,256
You are the worst!

76
00:04:58,923 --> 00:05:00,633
Didn't mean to poke the bear.

77
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:02,051
Whatever! Go to hell!

78
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,931
Ugh! Argh!
I can't believe I've sunk so low

79
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:10,184
that I'm being lumped in
with Mr. Pin right now.

80
00:05:10,268 --> 00:05:12,562
Hey, welcome to the company of men.

81
00:05:12,645 --> 00:05:15,565
GIRLS' BATHROOM

82
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:22,572
What's that supposed to mean,
"pretty serious"?

83
00:05:23,573 --> 00:05:24,699
That guy.

84
00:05:24,782 --> 00:05:26,701
He's always talking out of his butt.

85
00:05:43,426 --> 00:05:44,552
Ayane, hey!

86
00:05:44,635 --> 00:05:47,388
What are you doing for Christmas?

87
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:49,182
Got plans?

88
00:05:57,440 --> 00:06:01,361
Let's see. I have nothing scheduled,
and it's not like I have a boyfriend.

89
00:06:01,444 --> 00:06:04,447
I'll just do that class thing
with Sawako and Chizu this year.

90
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:07,950
- And you? Think you'll--
- Why don't we spend Christmas together?

91
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:10,286
Just us.

92
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:19,212
I mean, all by ourselves.

93
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:32,600
- Oh, there you are! Hi, Kento.
- Where are we doing Christmas this year?

94
00:06:32,683 --> 00:06:36,104
- I think it'd be nice to try a new place.
- Uh, hi, Ayane.

95
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:38,773
Come on,
you should totally join us for Christmas.

96
00:06:38,856 --> 00:06:40,358
It'll be so fun!

97
00:06:40,942 --> 00:06:42,318
Thanks, but I have to pass.

98
00:06:42,402 --> 00:06:45,613
- Ah?!
- I'm already doing the class party.

99
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:47,865
Uh... But I...

100
00:06:48,866 --> 00:06:50,910
See ya. I hope you enjoy.

101
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:57,375
- Aw! Too bad.
- She would've had a good time!

102
00:06:59,669 --> 00:07:01,587
Wonder if she's still mad about that?

103
00:07:02,296 --> 00:07:05,466
After the ceremony,
let's go home and freshen up.

104
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:07,969
Where were you guys
thinking of meeting up later?

105
00:07:08,052 --> 00:07:09,137
- Hey...
- Huh?

106
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:13,141
I can't make it this Christmas.

107
00:07:19,021 --> 00:07:21,232
I'm signing up
for the class party this year.

108
00:07:21,899 --> 00:07:23,109
I'm sorry, girls.

109
00:07:23,192 --> 00:07:26,112
- No way!
- We'll be so lonely!

110
00:07:27,738 --> 00:07:29,323
So, the party. You goin'?

111
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:32,910
I'm gonna go, so...

112
00:07:33,494 --> 00:07:34,829
Okay! Fine!

113
00:07:34,912 --> 00:07:37,915
I'm not gonna bow out now just 'cause
I know you're gonna to be there too.

114
00:07:37,999 --> 00:07:38,833
I...

115
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:40,751
I'm goin' anyway.

116
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:42,128
Got it?

117
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:47,550
Good to know,
but that's not what I asked at all.

118
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:50,511
Huh? Whaddya mean?!

119
00:07:50,595 --> 00:07:52,388
All right. I get it.

120
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:54,974
So... will ya go with me?

121
00:08:05,109 --> 00:08:06,861
Oh-- Ch-- Chizu?

122
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:09,447
Okay, so how did I seem
during all that, Sawa?

123
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:11,616
Uh... you were freaked out, like...

124
00:08:11,699 --> 00:08:12,825
Like, this much.

125
00:08:12,909 --> 00:08:14,452
Argh! I knew it!

126
00:08:15,036 --> 00:08:18,581
Argh! I can't do this!
I mean it, it's impossible, this is nuts!

127
00:08:18,664 --> 00:08:20,791
My heart's racing!

128
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:24,253
I... I think I might really be into
this "love-life talk" stuff!

129
00:08:24,337 --> 00:08:25,171
Like, a lot!

130
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:28,007
Wait, that's a random thing to say
when nothing's happening!

131
00:08:28,090 --> 00:08:30,551
And besides, shouldn't you be worrying
more about your own--

132
00:08:30,635 --> 00:08:31,636
Uh!

133
00:08:32,512 --> 00:08:35,056
Well, it seems like you're doing okay.

134
00:08:35,139 --> 00:08:36,641
- Uh, no.
- Uh?

135
00:08:36,724 --> 00:08:40,811
Hmm, now that I think of it, it does seem
like something's been bothering Kazehaya.

136
00:08:40,895 --> 00:08:44,190
- Huh?
- Uh... was I not supposed to say that?

137
00:08:44,774 --> 00:08:47,193
Eh, well I don't think he told me not to.

138
00:08:47,276 --> 00:08:48,361
Look over there.

139
00:08:48,444 --> 00:08:51,322
See that?
It's like his mind is somewhere else.

140
00:08:51,405 --> 00:08:56,327
Wild, right? Joe's talkin' his ear off,
but he's not hearing a word he's saying.

141
00:08:56,410 --> 00:08:58,412
- Please!
- At least notice him, man!

142
00:08:58,496 --> 00:09:01,040
Joe can pretty much
babble like that forever, huh?

143
00:09:01,123 --> 00:09:04,335
- Just give up, already!
- So he's stressed?

144
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:16,806
What you thinkin' of gettin'
for the gift exchange?

145
00:09:16,889 --> 00:09:20,101
Uh, I guess something
like this should work? Yeah.

146
00:09:20,851 --> 00:09:24,021
- Uh, what's that giant lump?
- Rock salt!

147
00:09:24,105 --> 00:09:27,650
I knew I was right about things
feeling a little different than before.

148
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:30,444
He wasn't just being awkward around me!

149
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:32,280
Dummy, dummy, dummy.

150
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:35,992
-I'm such a dummyyyyy!
- So you're going with a bath bomb, huh?

151
00:09:36,826 --> 00:09:38,786
Getting Kazehaya something too?

152
00:09:38,869 --> 00:09:40,788
Yeah. I'm making it now.

153
00:09:40,871 --> 00:09:41,872
Course you are.

154
00:09:45,668 --> 00:09:47,837
So this is probably how it's gonna go.

155
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:51,424
Kazehaya's most likely
planning to go to the class party,

156
00:09:51,507 --> 00:09:54,218
then also do something else
with just the two of you.

157
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:55,845
Like, the day before or after.

158
00:10:00,308 --> 00:10:01,976
Maybe he is.

159
00:10:04,645 --> 00:10:05,479
Finished!

160
00:10:08,649 --> 00:10:10,443
Well, I hope he likes it.

161
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:16,115
What is it that's bothering him?

162
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:21,287
It didn't seem like Chizu
had any idea what it could be either.

163
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:22,371
I'll ask him.

164
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:24,832
Or maybe it's better if I don't.

165
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:26,500
Oh... but...

166
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:32,923
No. Maybe I should.

167
00:10:34,383 --> 00:10:36,594
I really want to be there for him.

168
00:10:37,386 --> 00:10:40,598
But is there anything I can do... to help?

169
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:51,901
Kuronuma, ready?

170
00:10:51,984 --> 00:10:54,070
Uh, um, Kazehaya.

171
00:10:54,153 --> 00:10:56,197
Can you come over here for a second?

172
00:10:56,822 --> 00:10:57,990
- Hmm?
- Follow me.

173
00:11:00,451 --> 00:11:01,535
Uh, what's goin' on?

174
00:11:02,703 --> 00:11:03,996
Well, um... it's just...

175
00:11:04,622 --> 00:11:06,290
Let's go some place more private.

176
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:11,253
Come on! This way!

177
00:11:11,337 --> 00:11:13,214
OFF-LIMITS

178
00:11:15,257 --> 00:11:16,967
Uh... what's up?

179
00:11:17,051 --> 00:11:18,469
I-- I, uh...

180
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:21,055
You see, I... I wanted to...

181
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:43,285
What's wrong?

182
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:45,454
I wanted to talk.

183
00:11:58,759 --> 00:12:01,262
Has something been... bothering you?

184
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:23,951
No.

185
00:12:30,583 --> 00:12:31,625
I see.

186
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:37,173
Maybe... I completely misread things.

187
00:12:47,391 --> 00:12:49,560
- Bye.
- Yeah.

188
00:13:25,054 --> 00:13:26,347
That was scary.

189
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:29,058
I wanted to talk.

190
00:13:32,186 --> 00:13:34,438
I really thought
she was gonna break up with me.

191
00:13:36,857 --> 00:13:39,026
Has something
been bothering you?

192
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:43,030
This is exactly why
I can't say anything to Yoshida!

193
00:13:49,036 --> 00:13:50,704
Something on my mind?

194
00:13:53,707 --> 00:13:55,209
These would look good on her.

195
00:13:57,253 --> 00:13:58,379
Like what?

196
00:14:00,714 --> 00:14:03,384
Kazehaya. Kazehaya.

197
00:14:03,467 --> 00:14:04,593
Kazehaya!

198
00:14:05,886 --> 00:14:07,888
Hi. It's been a while, huh?

199
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:10,224
Y-- yes, it has, sir!

200
00:14:10,307 --> 00:14:11,600
Good afternoon to you!

201
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:14,270
N-- no, wait, it's dark already,
so good evening.

202
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:17,648
Wh-- what are the odds,
us bumping into each other here like this?

203
00:14:17,731 --> 00:14:21,277
Oh! Out shopping
for a present for a girl, perhaps?

204
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:24,655
- I-- it's for Kuronuma, of course!
- Of course.

205
00:14:24,738 --> 00:14:27,658
- What did you pick out for her?
- I still haven't decided yet.

206
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:30,703
Well, don't even think about a scarf.
I've got that all covered.

207
00:14:30,786 --> 00:14:33,080
Speaking of covered,
take a look at this thing!

208
00:14:33,163 --> 00:14:35,291
It's from Sawako. Handmade!

209
00:14:35,374 --> 00:14:37,001
It's pretty lit, huh?

210
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:39,670
Y-- yes, sir. It's... "lit."

211
00:14:40,963 --> 00:14:43,340
He scared me half to death!

212
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:47,469
You and Sawako... are officially a couple.

213
00:14:47,553 --> 00:14:49,263
That's true, right?

214
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:53,267
Yes.

215
00:14:53,767 --> 00:14:56,687
I see.

216
00:14:57,646 --> 00:15:00,316
So what will you two
be doing for Christmas?

217
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:02,693
Uh, we don't really
have plans, but...

218
00:15:02,776 --> 00:15:04,778
Oh! Right! Course not!

219
00:15:04,862 --> 00:15:06,322
I already heard all about it.

220
00:15:06,405 --> 00:15:10,242
Your class is planning to get together
for a big party on the 24th, right?

221
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:12,161
See, her mother... I mean, my wife says

222
00:15:12,244 --> 00:15:16,373
that Sawako would probably wanna spend
the holiday with her boyfriend, with you,

223
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,667
and that we shouldn't
get in the way of your plans.

224
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:22,922
But, you know, I haven't heard a single
peep about anything like that from Sawako.

225
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:26,091
And whenever I ask her,
she just says, "Don't be silly!"

226
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:28,177
So, um, in other words, I mean,

227
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:30,763
you're not planning anything
just the two of you?

228
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:33,474
- No, sir.
- Huh?

229
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:37,811
Well, actually... we'll be with everyone.

230
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:41,273
Uh... I-- I see.

231
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,233
That's wonderful!

232
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:45,694
Wow! That just makes me so happy to hear!

233
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:48,072
Don't catch a cold!

234
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:58,999
Maybe this really is for the best.

235
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:02,920
- Hey, who's that short old guy?
- Miura!

236
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:05,339
- What are you doing here?
- Huh?

237
00:16:05,923 --> 00:16:08,759
Obviously shopping
for a present for a girl.

238
00:16:08,842 --> 00:16:11,136
I've looked in all these stores,
but no luck.

239
00:16:11,929 --> 00:16:14,640
Also, I have no clue
what would make her happy.

240
00:16:19,019 --> 00:16:21,146
Hey. Let's get some tea.

241
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:22,147
Huh?!

242
00:16:26,068 --> 00:16:28,487
Ah, so that guy was actually Sadako's dad.

243
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:31,365
Wow! That must have been
a total nightmare for you.

244
00:16:31,991 --> 00:16:33,701
What's the deal today?

245
00:16:37,454 --> 00:16:39,873
It's been nothing but pure chaos.

246
00:16:39,957 --> 00:16:41,500
Yeah, if I'm gonna be honest,

247
00:16:41,583 --> 00:16:44,753
I never expected you to actually agree
to come and have tea with me, ya know?

248
00:16:44,837 --> 00:16:45,671
Huh?

249
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:49,591
I mean... you did wanna talk, right?

250
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:03,272
Y'see, there's this girl I'm falling for.

251
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:07,568
She's mine.

252
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:19,455
- I'm not talking about Sadako!
- So why are you telling me about it, then?

253
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:20,539
That's awesome, man.

254
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:23,333
It'd be better if you said it
in front of Sadako though, she'd love it!

255
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:24,251
- Wha--
- Hold on!

256
00:17:24,334 --> 00:17:26,754
We could totally reenact it for her later.
What do you think?

257
00:17:26,837 --> 00:17:29,506
Argh! Stop and get to the point, would ya?

258
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:31,467
Oh boy.

259
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:34,595
How is it that you can figure out
that I have something to say,

260
00:17:34,678 --> 00:17:36,930
but you have no idea
who I'm talking about?

261
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:42,978
But, man, Sadako must really
mean the world to you, huh?

262
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:45,189
The world.

263
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:48,984
But yeah, I actually did
wanna ask you about something.

264
00:17:50,486 --> 00:17:51,320
Ayane.

265
00:17:54,364 --> 00:17:56,116
That's the girl that I like.

266
00:17:58,702 --> 00:18:01,163
It's not like
I've never gotten any pushback

267
00:18:01,246 --> 00:18:03,415
from a girl I liked before or anything.

268
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:04,500
But it's different.

269
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:13,008
Or... maybe I've just never tried
to reach for something that felt

270
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:15,260
so beyond my grasp before.

271
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:21,308
I reached out, and we finally...

272
00:18:27,022 --> 00:18:27,981
But...

273
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:31,151
even when I do reach out, she runs away.

274
00:18:31,944 --> 00:18:34,363
She never lets her guard down.
She's bulletproof.

275
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:38,534
So why does she have
so little self-confidence?

276
00:18:39,243 --> 00:18:41,495
Maybe it's just the mask she hides behind.

277
00:18:43,247 --> 00:18:45,332
What can I do to get my foot in the door?

278
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:47,584
Getting a present's tough.

279
00:18:47,668 --> 00:18:51,338
I have no idea what she really likes,
so I don't know what to get her.

280
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:52,714
And that sucks, ya know?

281
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:56,635
Or is all of this just... crazy?

282
00:18:57,678 --> 00:18:59,513
No. I get it.

283
00:19:04,143 --> 00:19:05,519
I don't know what,

284
00:19:05,602 --> 00:19:08,772
but I can tell that something in her past
must have really hurt her.

285
00:19:09,898 --> 00:19:12,734
Do you know anything
about Ayane's past boyfriends?

286
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:15,279
No, not really.

287
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:20,659
One time, she did come to school
with her cheek all swollen.

288
00:19:24,746 --> 00:19:26,415
No! Why?!

289
00:19:27,249 --> 00:19:29,585
Why were you dating
someone like that, Ayane?!

290
00:19:29,668 --> 00:19:30,627
It makes no sense!

291
00:19:30,711 --> 00:19:33,964
Not when I could... give you so much more.

292
00:19:34,631 --> 00:19:37,176
A relationship that's full of good times,

293
00:19:37,259 --> 00:19:38,594
I could give that to her.

294
00:19:38,677 --> 00:19:40,387
I'd be there for her.

295
00:19:40,470 --> 00:19:42,389
And I'd treat her like a queen!

296
00:19:42,472 --> 00:19:44,683
What the hell is wrong
with these men lately?

297
00:19:45,267 --> 00:19:48,770
Including you! It was happening
in front of you, and you did nothing?

298
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:49,688
I'm sorry!

299
00:19:51,690 --> 00:19:52,524
No.

300
00:19:53,358 --> 00:19:54,193
That's not...

301
00:19:55,652 --> 00:19:58,697
Right now, I'm... the problem.

302
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:00,282
Yeah.

303
00:20:00,782 --> 00:20:02,201
I am, yeah.

304
00:20:02,284 --> 00:20:03,118
Me.

305
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:15,380
So how have things been goin'?

306
00:20:15,464 --> 00:20:16,798
- Y'know, with Sadako.
- Mm?

307
00:20:16,882 --> 00:20:19,218
Things do seem a little strained
between the two of you.

308
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:21,678
Never mind. Forget that I said that.

309
00:20:22,387 --> 00:20:25,474
What I actually meant to ask
was how you managed to get Sadako

310
00:20:25,557 --> 00:20:28,143
to get comfortable enough
to really open up to you.

311
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:31,605
I mean, do you think it's that
"wholesome" vibe thing you got goin' on?

312
00:20:31,688 --> 00:20:33,440
What do you think of my energy?

313
00:20:33,523 --> 00:20:34,691
Am I wholesome?

314
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:37,152
Huh?

315
00:20:37,861 --> 00:20:40,948
I'm not... particularly wholesome though.

316
00:20:42,115 --> 00:20:44,076
And do I really have to be?

317
00:20:45,661 --> 00:20:48,664
But, what does that
even mean, "wholesome"?

318
00:20:49,915 --> 00:20:53,794
Because I... I'm nothing like that. At all.

319
00:20:55,170 --> 00:20:57,881
I'm just not the person
everybody thinks I am.

320
00:20:58,507 --> 00:21:01,718
Probably not what Kuronuma thinks either.

321
00:21:06,014 --> 00:21:11,645
- Come on. You really think so?
- She means the world to me. She does, but...

322
00:21:13,563 --> 00:21:18,610
It feels like she has this image of me
that I'm afraid I just can't maintain.

323
00:21:19,778 --> 00:21:23,573
I want to cherish her...
but how far do I go?

324
00:21:23,657 --> 00:21:26,451
And what if I make her think that I don't?

325
00:21:27,911 --> 00:21:30,205
And I'm pretty sure
she doesn't have a clue

326
00:21:31,498 --> 00:21:33,458
that I'm actually like this.

327
00:21:36,962 --> 00:21:41,341
Huh.
Maybe I had the wrong idea about you.

328
00:21:43,343 --> 00:21:46,430
You and Sadako are so... similar.

329
00:21:53,729 --> 00:21:55,605
No one's said that before.

330
00:21:58,233 --> 00:22:00,485
Bye! If you ever need to unload again,

331
00:22:00,569 --> 00:22:02,821
just let me know,
and I'll be there for you.

332
00:22:02,904 --> 00:22:05,407
Was I the one
who started the conversation?

333
00:22:17,169 --> 00:22:20,255
Sadako, who's always
been branded as, well, "Sadako,"

334
00:22:20,881 --> 00:22:23,592
and Kazehaya, who's always
been branded as "wholesome."

335
00:22:24,926 --> 00:22:29,473
I guess he's trying to rebrand himself
as just "Kazehaya" right now.

336
00:22:31,350 --> 00:22:33,727
Even though neither of them
can see it that way.

337
00:22:37,314 --> 00:22:38,774
Welcome home, Dad!

338
00:22:38,857 --> 00:22:41,610
Hi, Sawako! I ran into Kazehaya.

339
00:22:42,194 --> 00:22:44,196
Oh yeah? B-- but where?

340
00:22:44,279 --> 00:22:46,782
Oh! I can't tell you that!

341
00:22:47,532 --> 00:22:49,534
We talked about that other thing though.

342
00:22:49,618 --> 00:22:52,371
He said your whole class
will be together on the 24th,

343
00:22:52,454 --> 00:22:55,916
but you two have no plans
to do anything the day before or after.

344
00:22:55,999 --> 00:22:57,626
Yeah.

345
00:22:57,709 --> 00:23:01,421
So we'll do ours on the 25th!
It works out! Leave that day free for us.

346
00:23:03,215 --> 00:23:05,926
Sure.

347
00:23:06,009 --> 00:23:08,678
Then also do something else
with just the two of you.

348
00:23:11,765 --> 00:23:14,017
He gently took my hand with his

349
00:23:15,727 --> 00:23:16,686
and then let it go.

350
00:23:26,238 --> 00:23:27,781
I had it all wrong.

351
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:32,035
I was wrong... about everything.

352
00:23:36,790 --> 00:23:39,876
I wasn't the one
who was putting distance between us,

353
00:23:41,169 --> 00:23:43,130
it was Kazehaya this whole time.

354
00:23:48,427 --> 00:23:49,678
So here's the spiel.

355
00:23:49,761 --> 00:23:52,305
Christmas and New Year's
are just around the corner,

356
00:23:52,806 --> 00:23:55,809
but there better not be any fighting
or drinking or smoking, got it?

357
00:23:55,892 --> 00:23:57,978
No matter how you slice it,
you're all still minors.

358
00:23:58,562 --> 00:24:01,565
If you're planning to go on to college,
study as much as you need.

359
00:24:01,648 --> 00:24:03,608
Everyone else? Well, do what you want.

360
00:24:04,443 --> 00:24:05,402
Oh yeah!

361
00:24:05,485 --> 00:24:08,363
You've got that thing today, right?
The Christmas party?

362
00:24:08,447 --> 00:24:11,700
Well, make sure
you have yourselves plenty of fun.

363
00:24:11,783 --> 00:24:15,704
But you won't have nearly as much
as I'm gonna! And dismissed!

364
00:24:16,830 --> 00:24:19,875
- Winter break!
- The party starts at 6, okay?

365
00:24:21,793 --> 00:24:25,380
- Kazehaya! So for the party prep?
- All good.

366
00:24:25,464 --> 00:24:27,215
Andy and I are gonna go buy supplies.

367
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:29,551
Gotcha! I think I'll tag along
with you, then.

368
00:24:29,634 --> 00:24:31,928
You're gonna head
straight there from here, right?

369
00:24:32,012 --> 00:24:32,846
Yeah.

370
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:35,307
Uh...

371
00:24:36,683 --> 00:24:38,560
All right.

372
00:24:39,352 --> 00:24:40,812
I'll see ya.

373
00:24:42,147 --> 00:24:42,981
Sure.

374
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:51,448
Come to think of it, we parted ways
like this last year too, huh?

375
00:24:52,199 --> 00:24:55,702
Back when we were first-years,
we weren't dating yet,

376
00:24:55,785 --> 00:24:58,622
and we weren't able
to spend Christmas together at all.

377
00:24:59,289 --> 00:25:02,501
And, even though
we can spend it together this year...

378
00:25:07,339 --> 00:25:08,507
...why is it that

379
00:25:09,299 --> 00:25:11,176
I'm more anxious now?

380
00:25:12,552 --> 00:25:14,012
Oh, that reminds me.

381
00:25:14,095 --> 00:25:16,932
What did you end up buying
for the gift exchange, Chizu?

382
00:25:17,015 --> 00:25:18,475
I know you couldn't decide.

383
00:25:18,558 --> 00:25:21,394
I, uh,
still haven't found something.

384
00:25:21,478 --> 00:25:22,979
What? It's today!

385
00:25:23,563 --> 00:25:25,774
Trust me, I understand that, okay!

386
00:25:26,399 --> 00:25:30,028
What did you think was the purpose
of our little shopping trip the other day?

387
00:25:30,111 --> 00:25:32,614
For some reason,
I can't seem to make up my mind.

388
00:25:32,697 --> 00:25:36,576
I told you any single-use item would be
totally fine and to just buy whatever!

389
00:25:37,202 --> 00:25:40,580
Yeah, I know that. I know, but... Argh!

390
00:25:40,664 --> 00:25:44,209
Fine! Whatever! Screw it,
I'll get that one dumb thingy!

391
00:25:44,292 --> 00:25:46,962
Go on home! Bye-bye! I'll see you tonight!

392
00:25:48,797 --> 00:25:51,341
I think I might have
sent her over the edge.

393
00:25:51,424 --> 00:25:52,926
Y-- yeah, maybe.

394
00:25:53,510 --> 00:25:56,721
- And I wonder what "thingy" she meant?
- Mmm.

395
00:25:56,805 --> 00:25:57,889
Ayane!

396
00:26:04,354 --> 00:26:06,064
- Have a happy New Year.
- Whoa!

397
00:26:06,147 --> 00:26:08,275
Hold on! Not so fast!

398
00:26:09,234 --> 00:26:11,903
I'm gonna be
at the class get-together tonight.

399
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:15,907
What are you going to do
about the Kento Girls?

400
00:26:15,991 --> 00:26:17,075
Uh, "Kento Girls"?

401
00:26:17,158 --> 00:26:20,078
What are you talkin' about?
But I do like the sound of it.

402
00:26:20,161 --> 00:26:22,038
- You should be one.
- Yeah, no way.

403
00:26:22,831 --> 00:26:25,083
I feel like
that shot barely missed me.

404
00:26:26,710 --> 00:26:28,920
Anyway, I'll be there.

405
00:26:31,089 --> 00:26:32,757
Later.

406
00:26:32,841 --> 00:26:35,468
- C'mon, Sawako.
- Uh, okay.

407
00:26:35,552 --> 00:26:38,346
I'll see you later, then, master.

408
00:26:40,515 --> 00:26:41,975
So I'll see you there!

409
00:26:55,196 --> 00:26:57,907
- So what's your take on that?
- Huh?

410
00:26:57,991 --> 00:27:01,953
Kento. I've been wondering
if maybe he likes me.

411
00:27:03,872 --> 00:27:07,334
Yes, he absolutely does! But I can't say.

412
00:27:07,417 --> 00:27:09,419
I'm dying to tell you, but I can't!

413
00:27:10,003 --> 00:27:12,380
- Nah. That'd never happen.
- Huh?

414
00:27:13,214 --> 00:27:16,801
He always says what he thinks people
want to hear, but it's meaningless.

415
00:27:16,885 --> 00:27:17,927
They're just words.

416
00:27:18,011 --> 00:27:20,513
And I'm sure there's no way
he meant any of that.

417
00:27:21,264 --> 00:27:23,308
He is a good person.

418
00:27:25,894 --> 00:27:27,771
Yeah. I know that.

419
00:27:28,938 --> 00:27:31,232
Kento is a genuinely good guy.

420
00:27:31,316 --> 00:27:32,484
Maybe that's why.

421
00:27:33,026 --> 00:27:34,402
Every once in a while,

422
00:27:34,486 --> 00:27:37,656
I find myself wondering
if he really meant something he said.

423
00:27:39,282 --> 00:27:40,408
Huh?

424
00:27:41,284 --> 00:27:43,203
But there's no way he likes me.

425
00:27:45,246 --> 00:27:46,498
Why not?

426
00:27:49,542 --> 00:27:53,254
Sawako, hey.
You love Kazehaya, right?

427
00:27:53,963 --> 00:27:54,964
What's it feel like?

428
00:27:55,548 --> 00:27:56,383
Huh?

429
00:28:00,512 --> 00:28:01,763
I'm not sure.

430
00:28:04,140 --> 00:28:06,184
It's like I'm really happy.

431
00:28:07,060 --> 00:28:10,772
But also, always anxious and on edge.

432
00:28:12,774 --> 00:28:15,735
When Kazehaya's around, I can't breathe.

433
00:28:16,486 --> 00:28:19,239
I could be happy, I could be sad,

434
00:28:19,322 --> 00:28:22,617
I could be having fun,
or I could be worried,

435
00:28:22,701 --> 00:28:26,329
but my heart starts to pound,
and my chest feels tight.

436
00:28:26,913 --> 00:28:28,331
It's hard to explain.

437
00:28:29,290 --> 00:28:31,626
And I have no clue how he feels either.

438
00:28:33,211 --> 00:28:36,548
But even my own feelings are too much.

439
00:28:38,091 --> 00:28:42,303
If whatever's eating at him
is about us, what do I do?

440
00:28:42,387 --> 00:28:45,181
If he's having second thoughts,
what do I do?

441
00:28:45,724 --> 00:28:47,600
If he doesn't like me anymore,

442
00:28:48,268 --> 00:28:49,352
what do I do?

443
00:28:55,316 --> 00:28:59,070
I'm sorry. Sorry.

444
00:29:00,113 --> 00:29:02,031
Something's gotten into me.

445
00:29:02,574 --> 00:29:03,867
This is so strange.

446
00:29:04,826 --> 00:29:07,287
I just can't control myself.

447
00:29:07,370 --> 00:29:09,080
I'm sorry.

448
00:29:09,164 --> 00:29:11,207
I'm so sorry.

449
00:29:14,252 --> 00:29:16,463
Yeah. Me too.

450
00:29:17,464 --> 00:29:21,176
We're going through different things...
but I feel the same.

451
00:29:22,260 --> 00:29:25,346
And because yours is so different...
I'm jealous.

452
00:29:30,518 --> 00:29:31,561
I really am.

453
00:29:32,437 --> 00:29:33,813
I'm jealous of you, Sawako.

454
00:29:34,856 --> 00:29:37,859
Not just you. That goes for Chizu too.

455
00:29:38,777 --> 00:29:42,155
I see the two of you laugh,
and blush, and get those butterflies.

456
00:29:43,031 --> 00:29:44,324
And cry.

457
00:29:45,033 --> 00:29:49,162
You both have these confusing feelings,
but you still keep trying.

458
00:29:49,245 --> 00:29:50,371
And I'm jealous.

459
00:29:50,997 --> 00:29:52,791
I've never told anyone I like them.

460
00:29:53,541 --> 00:29:54,667
Nope. Never.

461
00:29:56,461 --> 00:30:00,298
Until now...
I've just kinda been going with the flow.

462
00:30:00,381 --> 00:30:03,176
I let the other person's emotions
dictate what I do.

463
00:30:07,055 --> 00:30:10,183
Sawako, back when
I was going out with Mogi,

464
00:30:10,266 --> 00:30:13,019
you asked me
when I realized that I liked him.

465
00:30:13,102 --> 00:30:13,978
Remember that?

466
00:30:14,687 --> 00:30:15,522
Uh-huh.

467
00:30:17,232 --> 00:30:21,611
See, the thing is, that thought
had never even crossed my mind before.

468
00:30:21,694 --> 00:30:23,446
He really blindsided me.

469
00:30:24,072 --> 00:30:25,573
It took me by surprise.

470
00:30:27,742 --> 00:30:30,286
Dealing with other girls
always meant competition.

471
00:30:31,079 --> 00:30:33,164
But being with guys was easier.

472
00:30:34,499 --> 00:30:36,292
- Really?
- Yeah.

473
00:30:37,043 --> 00:30:39,254
Probably made things easier for them too.

474
00:30:40,421 --> 00:30:43,049
What they want from me is pretty obvious.

475
00:30:43,132 --> 00:30:45,343
And all I have to do is give that to them.

476
00:30:46,553 --> 00:30:49,180
But that eventually gets old, you know?

477
00:30:49,848 --> 00:30:51,182
Because I don't love them.

478
00:30:55,436 --> 00:30:58,773
After a while, it starts to feel
like every guy'll be the same.

479
00:31:01,818 --> 00:31:02,902
I can't help it.

480
00:31:04,070 --> 00:31:04,988
That's how I feel.

481
00:31:06,197 --> 00:31:09,784
So, when I slip up
and take Kento at his word,

482
00:31:09,868 --> 00:31:12,453
I get hit with all sorts of emotions,

483
00:31:12,537 --> 00:31:14,956
and I have no idea what to do anymore.

484
00:31:16,082 --> 00:31:17,292
What should I do?

485
00:31:18,084 --> 00:31:19,460
And what do I want?

486
00:31:20,169 --> 00:31:23,464
Do I want a boyfriend or to fall in love?

487
00:31:24,173 --> 00:31:25,341
Am I into him?

488
00:31:26,092 --> 00:31:27,427
Am I not into him?

489
00:31:28,678 --> 00:31:29,679
Have I given up?

490
00:31:31,055 --> 00:31:32,473
Or do I still have hope?

491
00:31:34,726 --> 00:31:37,437
Will I eventually be able to fall for him?

492
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:38,479
Who knows.

493
00:31:39,188 --> 00:31:40,732
Maybe it's impossible.

494
00:31:43,568 --> 00:31:47,488
There's no one that I understand less
or am more frustrated with, than myself.

495
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:58,082
Urgh! Sorry! Somehow I ended up
going on a self-absorbed rant.

496
00:31:58,166 --> 00:32:02,003
Okay. So, Sawako,
we were talking about Kazehaya.

497
00:32:02,629 --> 00:32:03,963
I'm so sorry.

498
00:32:04,047 --> 00:32:07,091
When I started thinking about
how you really, truly love him,

499
00:32:07,175 --> 00:32:09,010
I suddenly got all jealous.

500
00:32:09,802 --> 00:32:13,765
I'm not worried about you guys.
But still, I'm here.

501
00:32:14,599 --> 00:32:17,435
She always tries so hard
to help others.

502
00:32:19,145 --> 00:32:21,064
You're so wrong.

503
00:32:21,648 --> 00:32:25,234
This girl who's so kind,
who I love so much.

504
00:32:25,318 --> 00:32:26,611
That's not true!

505
00:32:28,446 --> 00:32:29,280
It's not!

506
00:32:29,864 --> 00:32:31,616
I know that for a fact!

507
00:32:32,742 --> 00:32:36,037
She honestly thinks that
no one genuinely cares for her.

508
00:32:37,205 --> 00:32:40,416
Everyone would love you
if they really knew you.

509
00:32:41,167 --> 00:32:42,126
She doesn't see it.

510
00:32:43,044 --> 00:32:45,672
Ayane, who can do anything
she sets her mind to.

511
00:32:46,214 --> 00:32:49,634
But everyone who does know you,
loves you.

512
00:32:50,635 --> 00:32:53,429
How can she not know how amazing she is?

513
00:32:57,350 --> 00:33:00,478
So, you're telling me,
I'm the one you're crying over?

514
00:33:00,561 --> 00:33:01,396
You're sweet.

515
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:05,483
It's not that. You're the one
who's always been so sweet and kind.

516
00:33:06,275 --> 00:33:09,195
Oh, come on.
That's only because you're kind, Sawako.

517
00:33:09,779 --> 00:33:13,366
I mean, everyone's
a much better person for knowing you.

518
00:33:14,701 --> 00:33:17,704
No, that's not true.
Not at all!

519
00:33:19,288 --> 00:33:20,373
Thank you though.

520
00:33:20,957 --> 00:33:24,794
Actually, I'm not really
the person that you think I am.

521
00:33:24,877 --> 00:33:27,880
But either way, I know you mean that
with your whole heart,

522
00:33:27,964 --> 00:33:29,382
so I do believe you.

523
00:33:31,467 --> 00:33:32,844
My whole life,

524
00:33:33,428 --> 00:33:38,391
the only people I've connected with
are Chizu and then you, Sawako.

525
00:33:40,476 --> 00:33:44,313
If I'm being honest with you,
both of you are my heroes.

526
00:33:48,484 --> 00:33:51,988
That's the first time
I've ever said something like that.

527
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:59,662
Well, I'll see you in a bit.

528
00:34:08,046 --> 00:34:10,256
I'm sorry, Sawako.

529
00:34:11,507 --> 00:34:13,176
That made me happy.

530
00:34:13,259 --> 00:34:14,260
I love you.

531
00:34:15,678 --> 00:34:17,805
But I can't be fixed.

532
00:34:19,265 --> 00:34:22,685
I'm... the absolute worst.

533
00:34:23,644 --> 00:34:26,856
It fills a void
that no girl ever could!

534
00:34:30,068 --> 00:34:31,110
That's not...

535
00:34:31,819 --> 00:34:32,695
...true.

536
00:34:34,822 --> 00:34:36,449
They both said the same thing.

537
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:40,787
But... Kento would be the easy way out.

538
00:34:41,412 --> 00:34:43,831
He's a good guy. I just can't.

539
00:34:55,176 --> 00:34:58,179
I can't get through. Not me.

540
00:34:58,805 --> 00:35:00,014
Not with words.

541
00:35:01,641 --> 00:35:05,561
There's just a much bigger barrier...
that Ayane built

542
00:35:06,312 --> 00:35:08,314
'cause she's unable to accept herself.

543
00:35:22,829 --> 00:35:24,664
Sawa! Hey, over here!

544
00:35:30,294 --> 00:35:32,463
This one's our room, right?
Go on in!

545
00:35:33,673 --> 00:35:35,216
Oh, thank y--

546
00:35:36,926 --> 00:35:37,885
Ladies first.

547
00:35:40,388 --> 00:35:43,182
What did you finally buy
for the gift exchange, Chizu?

548
00:35:43,266 --> 00:35:45,351
Well, I, uh...

549
00:35:46,978 --> 00:35:47,812
Huh?

550
00:35:48,396 --> 00:35:51,482
It's nothing special.
Not even worth mentioning really.

551
00:35:51,566 --> 00:35:53,025
Go. Walk in.

552
00:35:54,527 --> 00:35:57,321
Chizu! Sawako! Let's sit over here!

553
00:36:00,324 --> 00:36:02,493
Kazehaya! We're gonna save you
a seat, okay?

554
00:36:12,879 --> 00:36:13,963
All right, then.

555
00:36:14,463 --> 00:36:16,799
Welcome, Class 2-D and plus-ones.

556
00:36:16,883 --> 00:36:19,093
Let's get this Christmas party started.

557
00:36:19,635 --> 00:36:20,469
Whaddya say?

558
00:36:21,053 --> 00:36:23,472
Cheers!

559
00:36:27,727 --> 00:36:30,188
Does everyone over there
already have a plate?

560
00:36:30,271 --> 00:36:31,689
They're comin' around!

561
00:36:32,398 --> 00:36:34,108
I'm collecting
the presents, guys.

562
00:36:34,192 --> 00:36:36,903
Be passing them around soon,
so just put them in here.

563
00:36:36,986 --> 00:36:38,029
Huh?

564
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:41,407
Oh! Joe spilled his...

565
00:36:41,490 --> 00:36:42,325
Joe!

566
00:36:42,408 --> 00:36:44,952
Uh... I got you some tissues.

567
00:36:45,036 --> 00:36:46,829
And... Hey, could you help him out?

568
00:36:46,913 --> 00:36:50,208
- Yeah, sure.
- I just bought these!

569
00:36:50,291 --> 00:36:53,544
- They were brand-new.
- How'd this even happen? Honestly.

570
00:36:57,173 --> 00:36:59,383
- Don't just sit there! Help me!
- Ow.

571
00:37:05,932 --> 00:37:07,558
- Don't look at me!
- Ow.

572
00:37:08,309 --> 00:37:09,852
So what do you want me to do?

573
00:37:09,936 --> 00:37:11,938
I... don't know!

574
00:37:12,021 --> 00:37:14,774
I feel bad for him. Yikes.

575
00:37:14,857 --> 00:37:17,443
Those two sure are comfortable
with each other, huh?

576
00:37:18,903 --> 00:37:20,571
Yes, thank you.

577
00:37:20,655 --> 00:37:23,324
Could we get more damp cloths?
Okay, thanks.

578
00:37:34,502 --> 00:37:35,336
Sadako!

579
00:37:36,087 --> 00:37:37,797
Hey! Time to put in a song.

580
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:39,298
It's your turn.

581
00:37:39,382 --> 00:37:42,260
We really wanna hear you
sing a song next, Sadako.

582
00:37:42,343 --> 00:37:43,552
Please sing for us!

583
00:37:44,136 --> 00:37:46,389
We wanna hear you
sing your song, Sadako!

584
00:37:46,472 --> 00:37:47,765
Please sing!

585
00:37:57,149 --> 00:37:59,318
Huh? Why's it so creepy?

586
00:37:59,819 --> 00:38:01,195
- Uh?
- What's going on?

587
00:38:01,279 --> 00:38:02,405
Uh...

588
00:38:03,531 --> 00:38:04,573
- Oh.
- What?

589
00:38:04,657 --> 00:38:06,659
- Is she gonna sing?
- Oh, okay.

590
00:38:06,742 --> 00:38:08,035
I didn't know she could.

591
00:38:08,953 --> 00:38:11,205
I'm not very good, but...

592
00:38:13,374 --> 00:38:18,629
♪ Life is all about ♪

593
00:38:19,171 --> 00:38:21,674
♪ Supporting one another... ♪

594
00:38:21,757 --> 00:38:25,052
- This is the song she picked out?
- That's as un-Christmassy as you can get.

595
00:38:25,136 --> 00:38:30,224
♪ My body creaks as many times ♪

596
00:38:30,850 --> 00:38:33,602
♪ As there are holes in the ground ♪

597
00:38:33,686 --> 00:38:36,022
Whoo! Yeah!

598
00:38:36,814 --> 00:38:41,235
- ♪ I dig one more hole ♪
- Yeah, dig it!

599
00:38:41,319 --> 00:38:42,945
Hey, Kazehaya.

600
00:38:43,029 --> 00:38:45,406
Our presents are supposed to go
in the box, right?

601
00:38:45,489 --> 00:38:47,491
Uh... Oh, yeah.

602
00:38:47,575 --> 00:38:48,534
Okay!

603
00:38:49,243 --> 00:38:52,288
Kazehaya! Hey, come join us
over here for a second.

604
00:38:52,371 --> 00:38:53,205
Sure.

605
00:38:54,248 --> 00:38:57,168
- ♪ I dig a third hole... ♪
- A third!

606
00:38:57,752 --> 00:39:00,671
Hey, man. Organizing all this
must have been rough.

607
00:39:00,755 --> 00:39:03,674
- ♪ I dig a fourth hole ♪
- What's this? A fourth hole!

608
00:39:03,758 --> 00:39:05,134
Am I right?

609
00:39:06,469 --> 00:39:10,931
-♪ Each time I dig a hole, tears flow ♪
- Another hole and more tears!

610
00:39:11,807 --> 00:39:14,894
- ♪ La la la la laaa ♪
- Now put your hands in the air!

611
00:39:21,067 --> 00:39:23,861
Good job, girls. Really amazing!

612
00:39:23,944 --> 00:39:26,322
I wasn't expecting
Chizu's background vocals.

613
00:39:26,405 --> 00:39:28,115
What can I say? It got me hyped.

614
00:39:28,199 --> 00:39:30,826
I'm so grateful
that you came up to help me out.

615
00:39:30,910 --> 00:39:32,620
I'm not... a good singer.

616
00:39:33,204 --> 00:39:36,040
If I was alone,
I might have brought down the whole mood.

617
00:39:36,123 --> 00:39:37,333
I don't know about that.

618
00:39:37,416 --> 00:39:40,419
It seems like that mysterious song
of yours is quite popular.

619
00:39:41,087 --> 00:39:46,384
♪ If you curse someone, dig two holes ♪

620
00:39:51,597 --> 00:39:53,808
Hey! Thanks for all this, Kazehaya.

621
00:39:53,891 --> 00:39:57,019
- Hoo! Busy guy, huh?
- Well, you could help, ya know?

622
00:39:57,103 --> 00:39:59,605
Nah, I think my talents
lie more with drinking.

623
00:39:59,688 --> 00:40:01,899
- Don't spill that one too.
- I won't!

624
00:40:07,029 --> 00:40:07,905
Hmm?

625
00:40:18,916 --> 00:40:20,459
Kazehaya!

626
00:40:21,043 --> 00:40:21,961
Yeah?

627
00:40:22,044 --> 00:40:24,922
Where do you want this?
After I've got all the presents.

628
00:40:25,005 --> 00:40:26,715
Should I just leave it right here?

629
00:40:26,799 --> 00:40:28,384
Oh, I'll show you.

630
00:40:31,137 --> 00:40:32,680
He's in charge, after all.

631
00:40:34,849 --> 00:40:37,893
Busy guy. And he's a hard worker too.

632
00:40:39,478 --> 00:40:40,354
Yeah.

633
00:40:41,564 --> 00:40:42,398
He is.

634
00:40:46,402 --> 00:40:49,071
He really is a good one, isn't he?

635
00:40:58,831 --> 00:41:00,583
Huh? Wha-- what?!

636
00:41:01,917 --> 00:41:02,960
Hold on.

637
00:41:03,043 --> 00:41:06,213
Are the couples m-- multiplying?

638
00:41:07,131 --> 00:41:09,133
But why?!

639
00:41:09,216 --> 00:41:11,510
Well,
because it's Christmas Eve.

640
00:41:11,594 --> 00:41:14,221
You and Kazehaya
are dating each other, right?

641
00:41:15,222 --> 00:41:19,518
How's that work? What do you do?
Like, when the two of you are all alone?

642
00:41:19,602 --> 00:41:23,022
- Uh... uh...
- Do you kiss and stuff-- Ouch!

643
00:41:23,105 --> 00:41:25,149
You need to learn when to shut up!

644
00:41:25,232 --> 00:41:28,611
Can you blame me?
Kazehaya never tells me anything!

645
00:41:28,694 --> 00:41:31,405
At this point, I kinda assumed
he was hiding that they were going out.

646
00:41:31,489 --> 00:41:32,781
Guys usually brag.

647
00:41:32,865 --> 00:41:35,534
You don't get to decide
what's normal or not for other people!

648
00:41:35,618 --> 00:41:37,036
What's the big deal?

649
00:41:37,119 --> 00:41:41,707
I don't have a girlfriend myself,
so I deserve a little bit of intel! Hm!

650
00:41:41,790 --> 00:41:44,627
He isn't talking about us, but...

651
00:41:45,878 --> 00:41:47,671
That's okay, right?

652
00:41:48,672 --> 00:41:52,301
We're still boyfriend
and girlfriend, aren't we?

653
00:41:52,384 --> 00:41:54,345
- Okay! Come on now...
- Hm.

654
00:41:54,428 --> 00:41:57,723
Let's not focus on other people.
Talk to me about your situation.

655
00:41:57,806 --> 00:42:00,267
Are you interested in anyone special?
Like a girl?

656
00:42:00,351 --> 00:42:03,604
Of course, there's a girl.
There's literally always a girl.

657
00:42:03,687 --> 00:42:07,191
There's no one on this planet who wants
a girlfriend more than this guy does!

658
00:42:07,274 --> 00:42:11,153
So, uh, Yano!
You are a strong candidate. Y'know?

659
00:42:11,237 --> 00:42:14,114
Incredible. Where does
this confidence of yours come from?

660
00:42:14,198 --> 00:42:15,616
I'm genuinely curious.

661
00:42:15,699 --> 00:42:17,076
'Cause... I'm me!

662
00:42:17,159 --> 00:42:18,160
Huh?

663
00:42:19,078 --> 00:42:20,371
You can't have her.

664
00:42:20,913 --> 00:42:22,081
I'm sorry.

665
00:42:24,667 --> 00:42:26,377
There is something you can do.

666
00:42:26,460 --> 00:42:28,546
But you need to change
your approach a little.

667
00:42:28,629 --> 00:42:30,548
How come? Why's she off limits?

668
00:42:31,131 --> 00:42:34,051
Try this. First you go up to a girl
that you really like,

669
00:42:34,134 --> 00:42:36,387
and then you ask her
what she honestly thinks about you.

670
00:42:36,470 --> 00:42:37,680
It works out well.

671
00:42:37,763 --> 00:42:40,724
'Cause she's unlikely
to say anything mean to your face.

672
00:42:40,808 --> 00:42:43,102
Then... just tell her
you're in love with her.

673
00:42:43,185 --> 00:42:44,562
Easy-peasy.

674
00:42:44,645 --> 00:42:47,439
Oh! Yes! Good! And then what? Yeah? What?

675
00:42:48,524 --> 00:42:49,817
So that's how it is.

676
00:42:49,900 --> 00:42:53,654
That's your approach with everyone?
Ask them what they think of you first?

677
00:43:01,620 --> 00:43:04,123
To be honest,
with you, I couldn't.

678
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:12,006
I told myself "no."

679
00:43:12,923 --> 00:43:14,174
Listen up, everyone!

680
00:43:14,258 --> 00:43:17,219
It's time to start the gift exchange!

681
00:43:17,303 --> 00:43:19,388
We're going to play some music,
and when it stops,

682
00:43:19,471 --> 00:43:21,557
whatever present you're holding is yours.

683
00:43:21,640 --> 00:43:24,602
And we'll break it up into five rounds.

684
00:43:26,312 --> 00:43:28,814
Wh-- what's the matter, Chizu?
Are you all right?

685
00:43:28,897 --> 00:43:32,109
Uh-- Oh! Uh, I-- I'm okay.

686
00:43:32,192 --> 00:43:35,404
Chizuru, what did you
end up buying for your gift?

687
00:43:35,487 --> 00:43:38,115
- Argh!
- Argh! Yoshida spilled her drink!

688
00:43:38,198 --> 00:43:39,700
That's not the point!

689
00:43:39,783 --> 00:43:42,620
It's all about
just enjoying the gift you've been given!

690
00:43:42,703 --> 00:43:45,331
Okay. I think I get it now.

691
00:43:48,792 --> 00:43:50,085
Okay, stop!

692
00:43:50,169 --> 00:43:52,254
I've never even seen this before.

693
00:43:54,381 --> 00:43:57,593
- Wha-- A tawashi scrubber brush?
- Hmm?

694
00:43:58,260 --> 00:44:01,055
Whoa! Looks like I got Kazehaya's.

695
00:44:01,138 --> 00:44:03,515
Huh-huh. Wonder what's inside?

696
00:44:03,599 --> 00:44:05,267
Oh--

697
00:44:05,351 --> 00:44:07,394
I'm...

698
00:44:09,563 --> 00:44:10,481
...jealous!

699
00:44:10,564 --> 00:44:13,359
Are you doin' okay, Sawako?

700
00:44:14,234 --> 00:44:16,820
- Uh, uh, uh, uh, uh.
- Uh?!

701
00:44:16,904 --> 00:44:18,197
There's a beast!

702
00:44:18,280 --> 00:44:20,866
An insatiable beast
dwelling deep inside my heart!

703
00:44:21,450 --> 00:44:22,785
Oh... kay.

704
00:44:22,868 --> 00:44:24,703
Guess I can take that as a "no"?

705
00:44:26,789 --> 00:44:30,334
Okay, it's gift exchange round 2.
Here we go!

706
00:44:32,419 --> 00:44:34,213
Am I gonna get one this time?!

707
00:44:34,296 --> 00:44:36,215
- What are you hoping for?
- Girlfriend!

708
00:44:38,384 --> 00:44:41,095
Music! Start!

709
00:45:04,535 --> 00:45:06,203
How are we feeling?

710
00:45:06,286 --> 00:45:07,496
Should I stop the music soon?

711
00:45:11,250 --> 00:45:14,461
- Oh! It's all up to you, Chizu.
- He-he!

712
00:45:14,545 --> 00:45:16,547
Sweeeet!

713
00:45:16,630 --> 00:45:18,257
Now, hurry up and pass it!

714
00:45:18,340 --> 00:45:19,925
Okay. Got it.

715
00:45:22,052 --> 00:45:24,263
- Here, Ryu.
- Hmm?

716
00:45:31,895 --> 00:45:33,480
- Ryu, pass!
- Hmm.

717
00:45:33,564 --> 00:45:35,149
- Huh!
- Stop!

718
00:45:35,232 --> 00:45:37,109
All right!

719
00:45:37,192 --> 00:45:40,237
Whoo! Him got one!
That's one point for Joe!

720
00:45:42,823 --> 00:45:46,076
I wonder what's inside it,
and more importantly, who's it from?

721
00:45:46,160 --> 00:45:48,996
That wrapping paper's cute.
So it's gotta be from a girl.

722
00:45:49,580 --> 00:45:51,415
Go on, open it up.

723
00:45:51,498 --> 00:45:53,375
- Okay!
- Oooo!

724
00:45:54,251 --> 00:45:55,419
Here goes!

725
00:45:57,212 --> 00:45:58,714
No! You can't!

726
00:46:00,215 --> 00:46:01,133
Mm--

727
00:46:15,731 --> 00:46:17,900
Waaaaaah!

728
00:46:17,983 --> 00:46:19,151
Chi-- Chizu?

729
00:46:20,027 --> 00:46:21,653
Oh, what should we--

730
00:46:21,737 --> 00:46:23,113
I've got this.

731
00:46:23,822 --> 00:46:24,782
Which coat is hers?

732
00:46:25,657 --> 00:46:27,993
- This one?
- Uh, y-- yes.

733
00:46:31,955 --> 00:46:34,249
That was my present!

734
00:46:34,333 --> 00:46:36,752
Ah. There, there.

735
00:46:37,336 --> 00:46:39,797
Hey, Kazehaya. Let me look real quick.

736
00:46:41,423 --> 00:46:42,257
There it is.

737
00:46:43,509 --> 00:46:44,676
Listen up, Joe.

738
00:46:44,760 --> 00:46:48,222
I'll give you this present.
It's from me, so stop crying, okay?

739
00:46:48,305 --> 00:46:50,224
Uh? From you to me?!

740
00:46:51,558 --> 00:46:52,810
What is it?

741
00:46:52,893 --> 00:46:55,229
It's, uh, one of those things.

742
00:46:55,312 --> 00:46:56,146
Yeah.

743
00:46:56,230 --> 00:46:58,357
It's a stone that brings you luck in love.

744
00:46:58,440 --> 00:47:00,734
If you pray to it every day,
then you'll get a girlfriend.

745
00:47:00,818 --> 00:47:03,695
- You'll be......my girlfriend now?!
- Not what I said.

746
00:47:05,072 --> 00:47:06,114
Chizu.

747
00:47:07,282 --> 00:47:08,742
What was in that present?

748
00:47:14,957 --> 00:47:17,376
It's-- it's cold!

749
00:48:12,472 --> 00:48:14,391
Hmm.

750
00:48:16,894 --> 00:48:18,854
- What are you doing?
- Who cares?!

751
00:48:19,438 --> 00:48:21,106
Don't say anything, just take it!

752
00:48:21,189 --> 00:48:22,357
It's yours! Hey!

753
00:48:22,441 --> 00:48:25,360
Why are you
opening it up right now?!

754
00:48:28,447 --> 00:48:31,575
I bought it for you, Ryu!

755
00:48:32,326 --> 00:48:33,744
It was always meant for you!

756
00:48:35,287 --> 00:48:36,204
I was hoping

757
00:48:36,914 --> 00:48:38,707
that you would end up with it.

758
00:48:39,291 --> 00:48:40,250
So...

759
00:48:40,334 --> 00:48:42,461
And before you say anything,
I get it, okay?

760
00:48:42,544 --> 00:48:43,629
I know what you're thinking!

761
00:48:43,712 --> 00:48:45,672
"What if I wasn't the one
who ended up getting it?"

762
00:48:45,756 --> 00:48:47,841
But I was, like, ya know,
"What if he does get it?"

763
00:48:47,925 --> 00:48:49,551
I mean, nobody could really know for sure.

764
00:48:49,635 --> 00:48:52,220
You might get it and you might not,
and that's just how it is.

765
00:48:53,096 --> 00:48:54,890
But you ended up almost getting it.

766
00:48:54,973 --> 00:48:56,224
You were this close!

767
00:48:56,308 --> 00:48:59,144
Although, I do kinda feel bad for Joe.

768
00:48:59,227 --> 00:49:00,729
A little. I guess.

769
00:49:01,313 --> 00:49:03,231
Argh! Are you even listening?

770
00:49:03,315 --> 00:49:04,149
Yeah.

771
00:49:04,942 --> 00:49:07,861
You were taking a chance on me.

772
00:49:09,988 --> 00:49:11,323
Thank you.

773
00:49:12,115 --> 00:49:13,116
Looks good?

774
00:49:15,077 --> 00:49:15,911
Mmm.

775
00:49:17,204 --> 00:49:19,623
The big doofus looks so happy.

776
00:49:19,706 --> 00:49:21,583
- I got something for you too.
- Huh?

777
00:49:23,502 --> 00:49:25,671
Outside of the exchange.

778
00:49:27,631 --> 00:49:29,007
Here. Open it.

779
00:49:36,390 --> 00:49:39,726
Mmm? Mm. Mmm. Mm-mm-mm-mm.

780
00:49:40,227 --> 00:49:42,104
Oh! There's the damn seam. Found it.

781
00:49:48,402 --> 00:49:51,446
Why did you
get me something like this?

782
00:49:51,530 --> 00:49:52,447
Huh?

783
00:49:54,825 --> 00:49:56,743
It doesn't remind you of yourself?

784
00:50:00,372 --> 00:50:02,541
Wha-- Like me, how?!

785
00:50:02,624 --> 00:50:06,044
Well......I don't really know
how to put it into words.

786
00:50:11,133 --> 00:50:14,344
A single pink rose? How is that like me?

787
00:50:14,428 --> 00:50:17,931
It's a... "preserved flower," they said.

788
00:50:18,015 --> 00:50:19,349
A "pre--" It's a what?

789
00:50:20,976 --> 00:50:24,354
I wonder. Is this the way Ryu sees me?

790
00:50:31,445 --> 00:50:33,280
Argh!

791
00:50:33,363 --> 00:50:34,781
Uh, let's go!

792
00:50:37,284 --> 00:50:38,118
Uh?

793
00:50:38,702 --> 00:50:39,536
Not yet.

794
00:50:40,120 --> 00:50:42,414
We haven't been alone like this
for a while.

795
00:50:43,790 --> 00:50:46,043
So let's make it last.

796
00:50:54,760 --> 00:50:57,429
Yoshida and Sanada
are takin' their sweet time.

797
00:50:57,512 --> 00:51:00,515
- Think maybe they're fighting?
- Joe, are you crying?

798
00:51:00,599 --> 00:51:03,769
Tears of joy.

799
00:51:04,936 --> 00:51:05,896
Chizu.

800
00:51:09,399 --> 00:51:12,861
No need to worry. Yoshida ran outside
without grabbing her coat,

801
00:51:12,944 --> 00:51:15,072
so Ryu decided to take it out to her.

802
00:51:15,155 --> 00:51:16,782
This stuff happens all the time.

803
00:51:16,865 --> 00:51:20,285
Yeah, Yoshida's almost always
acting without thinking first.

804
00:51:20,368 --> 00:51:22,245
Ryu's basically her caretaker.

805
00:51:22,329 --> 00:51:24,372
They could just be dating now?

806
00:51:25,957 --> 00:51:27,375
There's no way!

807
00:51:27,459 --> 00:51:29,294
Huh? Is it really that strange?

808
00:51:29,878 --> 00:51:32,964
She meant it for Ryu,
so that's why she panicked.

809
00:51:33,048 --> 00:51:35,801
And it explains
why she couldn't pick something.

810
00:51:35,884 --> 00:51:38,970
I mean, those two
need to just go out already.

811
00:51:40,555 --> 00:51:42,849
I think they're perfect for each other.

812
00:51:43,600 --> 00:51:46,394
I'm curious though, how Chizu feels.

813
00:51:47,562 --> 00:51:50,649
Well, those two are on their own planet.

814
00:51:50,732 --> 00:51:53,360
Maybe something's happening
no one would understand.

815
00:51:54,361 --> 00:51:56,029
Not that I'd have any clue.

816
00:51:56,780 --> 00:52:00,283
Oh, Ayane, your glass is empty.
Do you want something?

817
00:52:00,992 --> 00:52:04,037
Oh no. It's okay. I can get it myself.

818
00:52:11,211 --> 00:52:14,422
I'm so jealous of Sawako and Chizu.

819
00:52:22,305 --> 00:52:23,723
Sawako!

820
00:52:23,807 --> 00:52:28,228
Chizu, those feelings you just poured out,
does Ryu know?

821
00:52:28,812 --> 00:52:31,231
It's because you fought so hard for us.

822
00:52:31,314 --> 00:52:32,440
Have I given up?

823
00:52:33,733 --> 00:52:35,193
Or do I still have hope?

824
00:52:37,320 --> 00:52:40,699
Will I...
eventually be able to fall for him?

825
00:52:42,784 --> 00:52:44,202
Hmm?

826
00:52:44,286 --> 00:52:46,246
Wah! The heck did I step on?

827
00:52:46,329 --> 00:52:47,873
Argh!

828
00:52:47,956 --> 00:52:49,916
Huh? Uh, was it yours, Kento?

829
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:52,711
I'm sorry.
I stomped on it pretty hard too.

830
00:52:52,794 --> 00:52:55,505
Oh well,
that's not good.

831
00:52:55,589 --> 00:52:57,716
Is it okay?

832
00:52:57,799 --> 00:52:59,050
Uh, maybe?

833
00:52:59,134 --> 00:53:01,303
I'm gonna take a closer look to make sure.

834
00:53:10,145 --> 00:53:11,062
Oh.

835
00:53:11,897 --> 00:53:14,608
- Sadako.
- Oh, Master.

836
00:53:16,693 --> 00:53:18,904
You look kinda worried.
Is everything okay?

837
00:53:19,613 --> 00:53:21,281
I said she'd be fine, didn't I?

838
00:53:22,199 --> 00:53:24,075
Oh! Master!

839
00:53:24,159 --> 00:53:26,036
What is it? What happened?

840
00:53:26,119 --> 00:53:30,040
Or is Kazehaya
gonna be all upset with me again?

841
00:53:30,123 --> 00:53:33,543
I'm always thinking about my own problems.

842
00:53:33,627 --> 00:53:35,670
Even though everybody else has so many.

843
00:53:36,254 --> 00:53:38,465
Despite that, Ayane, she...

844
00:53:38,548 --> 00:53:41,968
She's always, no matter what... so kind.

845
00:53:42,761 --> 00:53:45,263
And I... I always idolized her.

846
00:53:45,347 --> 00:53:49,226
She's so mature, and I could
only see her as this perfect example.

847
00:53:49,309 --> 00:53:51,228
But... I was wrong.

848
00:53:51,311 --> 00:53:52,479
We're the same.

849
00:53:52,562 --> 00:53:53,980
We really are.

850
00:53:54,648 --> 00:53:58,693
For the first time,
I saw Ayane on the exact same level as me.

851
00:54:03,073 --> 00:54:07,452
Oh, it's no use.
I can't find the right words to explain.

852
00:54:08,662 --> 00:54:10,956
- I get it.
- Uh...

853
00:54:13,750 --> 00:54:15,460
Honestly.

854
00:54:16,920 --> 00:54:19,965
And I really
wanna make things better for her.

855
00:54:26,221 --> 00:54:27,806
Those stupid jerks!

856
00:54:27,889 --> 00:54:30,934
Can't believe they strung me along
like that! Nurse, my ass!

857
00:54:31,643 --> 00:54:34,271
What? You found a better
group of guys for the party?

858
00:54:34,354 --> 00:54:35,272
Argh!

859
00:54:36,231 --> 00:54:39,150
You guys are the worst! Huh?!

860
00:54:41,194 --> 00:54:42,821
Oh yeah! The brats are here!

861
00:54:42,904 --> 00:54:44,572
I need to blow off some steam!

862
00:54:44,656 --> 00:54:47,659
I have the uncontrollable desire
to mess with them right now!

863
00:54:49,452 --> 00:54:51,496
- Was that Pin?
- Uh-huh.

864
00:55:10,348 --> 00:55:12,851
- Wait, Mr. Arai?!
- Hmm? What the hell?!

865
00:55:12,934 --> 00:55:16,855
- You crazy, Kuronuma?! You scared me!
- I'm so sorry!

866
00:55:17,564 --> 00:55:18,690
Don't worry about it.

867
00:55:18,773 --> 00:55:21,484
You did nothing wrong,
so there's nothing to apologize for.

868
00:55:21,568 --> 00:55:23,737
S-- sorry, I won't! Huh.

869
00:55:23,820 --> 00:55:26,323
Not going in? How come?

870
00:55:26,990 --> 00:55:29,284
Well, it's just that, you know...

871
00:55:29,367 --> 00:55:30,410
Ha-ha!

872
00:55:30,493 --> 00:55:33,621
Let me guess, your brain's all fried
from overthinking something?

873
00:55:34,914 --> 00:55:36,833
I'll lend an ear.

874
00:55:36,916 --> 00:55:39,878
I bet it's something about Shota again,
am I right?

875
00:55:39,961 --> 00:55:41,463
Right! Then come with me.

876
00:55:41,546 --> 00:55:42,380
It's not!

877
00:55:42,464 --> 00:55:45,842
It's actually about me
since I only think of myself these days.

878
00:55:45,925 --> 00:55:48,345
And what's wrong with that?

879
00:55:48,428 --> 00:55:51,139
How are you supposed to
help anybody else with their problems

880
00:55:51,222 --> 00:55:52,766
if you don't have your own sorted?

881
00:55:52,849 --> 00:55:55,560
Well, you can't.

882
00:55:55,643 --> 00:55:57,896
Then, I think you found your answer, yeah?

883
00:55:58,646 --> 00:55:59,939
Oooooh!

884
00:56:00,023 --> 00:56:00,899
SCALE

885
00:56:01,566 --> 00:56:04,819
That reminds me,
I saw your Career Interest Survey.

886
00:56:04,903 --> 00:56:06,613
Are you sure that's what you want?

887
00:56:06,696 --> 00:56:07,864
Uh, sir?

888
00:56:07,947 --> 00:56:12,285
Listen... if that's what you honestly want
for yourself, then you should do you.

889
00:56:12,369 --> 00:56:14,454
You're not exactly
a selfless person, you know?

890
00:56:15,789 --> 00:56:17,332
So I am selfish!

891
00:56:17,415 --> 00:56:19,459
Come on. That was a compliment.

892
00:56:20,043 --> 00:56:20,877
Just sayin'.

893
00:56:20,960 --> 00:56:24,089
If something's important to you,
you go out and make it happen.

894
00:56:25,382 --> 00:56:27,175
If it's important to me.

895
00:56:30,970 --> 00:56:35,600
The thing is, maybe this whole time,
I've only done what I've wanted.

896
00:56:35,683 --> 00:56:38,645
I've had so many self-improvement plans.

897
00:56:38,728 --> 00:56:41,898
Like "Becoming the Person
I'm Doomed to Be, Part 1."

898
00:56:41,981 --> 00:56:44,234
Or "Smiling Practice, Part 1."

899
00:56:44,317 --> 00:56:49,614
But every single idea or intention...
was something that I wanted.

900
00:56:50,657 --> 00:56:54,411
I put everything into accomplishing
the things important to me.

901
00:56:54,494 --> 00:56:56,246
Even if it didn't work out.

902
00:56:56,329 --> 00:56:59,040
If I keep at it,
then maybe things will change.

903
00:56:59,124 --> 00:57:00,375
One day.

904
00:57:01,918 --> 00:57:06,423
But, then again... there's no guarantee
all that effort will amount to much.

905
00:57:07,757 --> 00:57:11,386
And now, I have so many people
who are dear to me,

906
00:57:11,469 --> 00:57:14,222
that I'm able to worry
about others for the first time.

907
00:57:16,015 --> 00:57:18,643
Not knowing what I can do to help them,

908
00:57:18,726 --> 00:57:21,813
not being able to keep
my own feelings under control,

909
00:57:22,772 --> 00:57:25,358
it's all because
I didn't understand myself,

910
00:57:25,859 --> 00:57:28,194
how many desires I truly had.

911
00:57:28,278 --> 00:57:31,865
Every day, it feels like there's
something new I can't put into words

912
00:57:31,948 --> 00:57:32,949
or even do.

913
00:57:35,702 --> 00:57:38,663
I want to know everything
about the person I love.

914
00:57:38,746 --> 00:57:42,250
I want everything about Kazehaya
to belong to me.

915
00:57:43,042 --> 00:57:45,211
But I can't have that.

916
00:57:46,838 --> 00:57:49,174
And it feels wrong for me to want it.

917
00:57:50,383 --> 00:57:52,010
I don't want to lose him.

918
00:57:53,094 --> 00:57:56,681
But, if I did, I have no idea what I'd do.

919
00:57:59,767 --> 00:58:02,312
- Ah! Well, that's better.
- Huh?

920
00:58:03,021 --> 00:58:06,649
You're thinkin' about your boyfriend
instead of being worried about yourself.

921
00:58:07,358 --> 00:58:10,445
Just the fact that you were able
to switch your emotions like that now

922
00:58:10,528 --> 00:58:12,489
means that none of this was pointless.

923
00:58:13,281 --> 00:58:14,741
I don't follow.

924
00:58:15,408 --> 00:58:18,411
I guess you haven't worked out
what to do about it quite yet.

925
00:58:19,496 --> 00:58:21,122
Okay, that's all for now!

926
00:58:21,206 --> 00:58:23,166
- Let's talk next semester!
- Oh.

927
00:58:24,292 --> 00:58:27,504
But, hey, when there's something
you wanna protect,

928
00:58:27,587 --> 00:58:30,548
it might seem like there are things
you need to avoid saying.

929
00:58:31,549 --> 00:58:33,718
But if you bottle up
all those feelings of yours,

930
00:58:33,801 --> 00:58:35,553
you'll only make yourself frustrated.

931
00:58:36,513 --> 00:58:40,016
Anyway, those feelings don't mean squat
in the grand scheme of things,

932
00:58:40,099 --> 00:58:41,518
so let 'em out!

933
00:58:41,601 --> 00:58:45,021
If you speak up, as stupid as that kid is,
he might get it.

934
00:58:45,104 --> 00:58:46,064
So just do it.

935
00:58:48,441 --> 00:58:50,068
You already know what to say.

936
00:58:50,151 --> 00:58:52,153
Just tell him exactly what you want.

937
00:58:53,988 --> 00:58:56,616
I can't do that...
and I shouldn't.

938
00:58:59,452 --> 00:59:02,914
But despite that... I want to.

939
00:59:05,667 --> 00:59:09,420
I knew it.
It got totally crushed.

940
00:59:14,759 --> 00:59:16,344
Oh, uh, Mogi?

941
00:59:16,928 --> 00:59:19,639
Let's see, it's like...
How do I put it?

942
00:59:19,722 --> 00:59:22,475
If you can do that,
he'll respect it right away.

943
00:59:23,184 --> 00:59:26,104
I know these things
because I'm such an attentive teacher.

944
00:59:26,187 --> 00:59:28,314
But what are you gonna do?

945
00:59:28,982 --> 00:59:32,652
Shota's always been tough.
It's 'cause he's so stubborn!

946
00:59:32,735 --> 00:59:35,196
As for exactly how stubborn he is,

947
00:59:35,780 --> 00:59:37,991
that boy's as stubborn
as a stubborn old man!

948
00:59:39,701 --> 00:59:42,453
Oh... he... is?

949
00:59:43,121 --> 00:59:46,833
Deep down, that kid can't rest
unless he gets exactly what he wants.

950
00:59:46,916 --> 00:59:48,042
He's his father's son.

951
00:59:49,085 --> 00:59:50,837
Oooooh!

952
00:59:52,463 --> 00:59:53,881
And, oh yeah, about Ryu?

953
00:59:53,965 --> 00:59:57,010
That guy has a really good heart
and a great big spirit.

954
00:59:57,093 --> 00:59:58,052
What do you mean?

955
00:59:58,136 --> 01:00:00,263
Are you dumb? That guy's crazy tough.

956
01:00:00,346 --> 01:00:02,015
Don't underestimate him.

957
01:00:02,098 --> 01:00:04,892
Then there's Yoshida.
Diligent, just in her own way.

958
01:00:04,976 --> 01:00:05,810
Yeah.

959
01:00:06,477 --> 01:00:09,022
She never comes to a test
totally unprepared.

960
01:00:09,105 --> 01:00:12,817
She's actually the type that stays up
to cram like crazy the night before.

961
01:00:13,526 --> 01:00:17,488
The problem is that she's not exactly
clever enough for that method to work out.

962
01:00:18,364 --> 01:00:21,868
Her, uh, self-awareness
is also not her strong suit.

963
01:00:22,410 --> 01:00:24,245
Uh, oh, really?

964
01:00:24,912 --> 01:00:27,999
You're Mogi from Class B, am I wrong?

965
01:00:28,708 --> 01:00:31,586
No, that's right, but...
Oh, you're in Class D.

966
01:00:31,669 --> 01:00:33,796
Ah yeah. For sure. I'm Kento.

967
01:00:33,880 --> 01:00:36,633
Oh yeah.
I totally remember who you are now.

968
01:00:36,716 --> 01:00:38,885
Well, see ya.

969
01:00:44,182 --> 01:00:48,144
That reminds me.
Miura too. He also has a pretty big heart.

970
01:00:48,227 --> 01:00:49,270
Yes.

971
01:00:50,104 --> 01:00:53,316
But he kinda makes me
wanna do something just to piss him off.

972
01:00:53,399 --> 01:00:55,943
That's a nasty face.

973
01:00:56,778 --> 01:00:58,488
Well, my work here's done.

974
01:00:58,571 --> 01:01:00,031
What about Ayane though?

975
01:01:01,199 --> 01:01:04,243
Huh... yeah.

976
01:01:05,286 --> 01:01:06,287
She's doing fine.

977
01:01:08,247 --> 01:01:09,082
But well...

978
01:01:11,542 --> 01:01:12,794
she's still a kid.

979
01:01:24,180 --> 01:01:26,391
Later, then.

980
01:01:29,185 --> 01:01:30,812
Hey! Hold on!

981
01:01:32,188 --> 01:01:34,315
You used to go out with Ayane, didn't you?

982
01:01:34,399 --> 01:01:36,275
Oh, uh... yeah.

983
01:01:37,360 --> 01:01:39,320
So what have we here?

984
01:01:39,904 --> 01:01:41,823
Looks like it's about to go down.

985
01:01:42,949 --> 01:01:44,784
W-- with Master?

986
01:01:45,326 --> 01:01:47,370
And... Mogi?

987
01:01:47,453 --> 01:01:49,997
We met during free time on Okinawa.

988
01:01:50,081 --> 01:01:52,834
- You remember that, don't you?
- Uh...

989
01:01:52,917 --> 01:01:55,670
Y'see, I... sorta ran into Ayane there.

990
01:01:57,755 --> 01:01:59,674
And she told me some stuff.

991
01:01:59,757 --> 01:02:02,176
Wait, Yano... she told you?

992
01:02:02,885 --> 01:02:03,803
Check it out.

993
01:02:03,886 --> 01:02:07,056
They have no idea we've been standing here
watching them this whole time.

994
01:02:07,140 --> 01:02:08,683
How spacey can you be?

995
01:02:08,766 --> 01:02:11,477
Uh, well, she didn't say anything.

996
01:02:11,978 --> 01:02:15,732
I was the one who asked her about it.
'Cause she was hurting.

997
01:02:15,815 --> 01:02:17,775
Look, you've got it wrong.

998
01:02:18,985 --> 01:02:19,986
It was...

999
01:02:20,528 --> 01:02:21,571
Yeah, no...

1000
01:02:22,405 --> 01:02:23,865
It worked out okay.

1001
01:02:23,948 --> 01:02:25,199
What do you mean by that?

1002
01:02:25,283 --> 01:02:29,787
Yano is...
actually mature, like a real adult.

1003
01:02:29,871 --> 01:02:31,539
I mean, she was cool with it.

1004
01:02:31,622 --> 01:02:34,208
I-- I did kind of feel guilty
after that, ya know?

1005
01:02:34,292 --> 01:02:36,836
What did you do?

1006
01:02:36,919 --> 01:02:39,839
Well, I didn't really "do" anything.

1007
01:02:39,922 --> 01:02:42,383
It's just, at the time...

1008
01:02:43,092 --> 01:02:46,387
Maybe I was expecting
a lot more from Yano than I should have?

1009
01:02:46,929 --> 01:02:48,139
Like what?

1010
01:02:48,848 --> 01:02:50,600
Expecting what?

1011
01:02:50,683 --> 01:02:52,185
Are you talking about sex or...

1012
01:02:53,770 --> 01:02:55,855
Did you do something to Ayane?

1013
01:02:55,938 --> 01:02:59,275
No, it wasn't like that.
Nothing happened, I swear. I kissed her.

1014
01:03:00,109 --> 01:03:01,110
That's all.

1015
01:03:01,694 --> 01:03:04,614
She was so mature about it.
And she forgave me.

1016
01:03:10,244 --> 01:03:13,956
So then, you had
all of these... expectations.

1017
01:03:14,040 --> 01:03:15,666
But did Ayane know about them?

1018
01:03:15,750 --> 01:03:18,503
Uh, hold on! Are you saying
she didn't tell you anything?

1019
01:03:20,004 --> 01:03:21,464
What happened?

1020
01:03:21,547 --> 01:03:26,052
The thing is, she overheard me
talking to the guys about us.

1021
01:03:26,886 --> 01:03:29,806
- I'm fine.
- I really am okay.

1022
01:03:30,389 --> 01:03:31,891
They were just curious.

1023
01:03:31,974 --> 01:03:35,353
They all wanted to know what it was like
to have a girlfriend, ya know?

1024
01:03:35,436 --> 01:03:38,147
- Like a report?
- Yeah, yeah!

1025
01:03:38,231 --> 01:03:39,315
But I lucked out.

1026
01:03:39,899 --> 01:03:42,819
When Yano walked up to us,
she didn't seem to be bothered.

1027
01:03:52,245 --> 01:03:55,331
Not bothered?
Are you kidding me?!

1028
01:03:56,123 --> 01:03:56,958
You're an idiot!

1029
01:03:57,583 --> 01:04:00,711
Why would you think it's okay
to tell people something so personal?

1030
01:04:01,462 --> 01:04:02,797
If I'm being honest,

1031
01:04:02,880 --> 01:04:06,843
I don't think any of the guys I dated
were really that into me anyway.

1032
01:04:06,926 --> 01:04:10,179
I'll ask you once more,
what did you do to her?

1033
01:04:10,263 --> 01:04:12,640
Seriously,

1034
01:04:12,723 --> 01:04:15,268
you're acting like
she disappointed you somehow!

1035
01:04:15,351 --> 01:04:20,147
But well, since I am the way I am,
I guess that's just a given.

1036
01:04:21,357 --> 01:04:22,733
It's mutual, right?

1037
01:04:24,402 --> 01:04:28,155
Did you think for even a second
that Ayane is more than that?

1038
01:04:28,865 --> 01:04:31,951
And to consider
how that made her feel?!

1039
01:04:37,415 --> 01:04:38,916
- Hey! Ayane!
- Huh?

1040
01:04:50,303 --> 01:04:52,555
Okay, that's enough.

1041
01:04:53,306 --> 01:04:56,684
Idiot. Didn't I tell you kids
not to get in any fights?

1042
01:04:58,436 --> 01:05:00,897
Hey, Mogi, you doin' all right?
Are you okay?

1043
01:05:00,980 --> 01:05:01,814
Uh, yeah.

1044
01:05:02,648 --> 01:05:05,067
I thought I heard fighting.
Down that way!

1045
01:05:05,151 --> 01:05:06,944
Hey. Kid. Now. Get outta here.

1046
01:05:07,528 --> 01:05:08,404
But I...

1047
01:05:08,487 --> 01:05:11,032
'Cause if you stay,
things'll just get complicated.

1048
01:05:11,115 --> 01:05:14,994
So head over there. The stairs.

1049
01:05:30,593 --> 01:05:32,303
Are you okay?

1050
01:05:45,608 --> 01:05:47,109
Um, excuse me?

1051
01:05:47,818 --> 01:05:51,238
We've gotten a number of complaints
about some sort of commotion out here.

1052
01:05:51,322 --> 01:05:53,866
Oh, don't worry about that! All good!

1053
01:05:53,950 --> 01:05:55,660
It's just this kid's a real klutz.

1054
01:05:55,743 --> 01:05:58,579
He slipped and fell flat
on his ass, that's all. Right?

1055
01:05:58,663 --> 01:06:00,247
Uh... y-- yeah.

1056
01:06:00,831 --> 01:06:02,875
All right, please be more careful, then.

1057
01:06:05,169 --> 01:06:06,045
Yano?

1058
01:06:08,881 --> 01:06:13,260
Sorry... about Okinawa.
I didn't realize it mattered that much.

1059
01:06:15,137 --> 01:06:18,057
I mean, I just figured...

1060
01:06:18,140 --> 01:06:22,061
'Cause, ya know... you didn't care that much
about me anyway.

1061
01:06:23,854 --> 01:06:27,024
But... it was awful of me, wasn't it?

1062
01:06:27,900 --> 01:06:29,235
I'm sorry.

1063
01:06:30,569 --> 01:06:33,280
Back when I first
bumped into you at school,

1064
01:06:33,364 --> 01:06:34,573
I liked you right away.

1065
01:06:34,657 --> 01:06:37,118
I thought, "Wow, this girl sure is great."

1066
01:06:38,077 --> 01:06:41,747
"I'd love to go out with her.
That would be so incredible, wouldn't it?"

1067
01:06:42,456 --> 01:06:45,292
And the upcoming school trip
gave me the kick I needed.

1068
01:06:45,376 --> 01:06:46,711
To work up the nerve.

1069
01:06:47,920 --> 01:06:50,006
I always let you take the lead.

1070
01:06:50,089 --> 01:06:52,842
And I never got the chance
to show you a good time.

1071
01:06:52,925 --> 01:06:54,385
And, yeah, it's true,

1072
01:06:55,302 --> 01:06:57,847
I definitely expected
certain things from you.

1073
01:06:59,932 --> 01:07:02,643
But I really did think
you were awesome and gorgeous.

1074
01:07:03,644 --> 01:07:04,687
Honestly.

1075
01:07:07,440 --> 01:07:08,274
Right.

1076
01:07:09,233 --> 01:07:11,819
- I can tell you're not lying about that.
- Uh.

1077
01:07:13,070 --> 01:07:13,904
You know what?

1078
01:07:13,988 --> 01:07:16,824
I really don't feel any hatred
towards you or anything.

1079
01:07:17,575 --> 01:07:21,829
Besides, it's not exactly your fault
that what you did hurt me so much.

1080
01:07:23,664 --> 01:07:25,583
It's okay.

1081
01:07:26,542 --> 01:07:28,878
I'm actually used to that stuff.

1082
01:07:28,961 --> 01:07:30,588
You don't need to say more.

1083
01:07:32,256 --> 01:07:34,508
- Thank you.
- Uh...

1084
01:07:35,593 --> 01:07:38,012
Have someone else
take care of your nose for you.

1085
01:07:41,807 --> 01:07:42,641
Hey.

1086
01:07:44,518 --> 01:07:47,021
Miura took the emergency stairs.

1087
01:07:58,741 --> 01:08:00,826
And that'll be his Christmas present.

1088
01:08:21,764 --> 01:08:22,848
Ayane, you...

1089
01:08:28,312 --> 01:08:30,773
What are you doing out here
dressed like that?

1090
01:08:30,856 --> 01:08:31,982
It's freezing.

1091
01:08:32,066 --> 01:08:34,068
- It's fine.
- It's totally not.

1092
01:08:42,743 --> 01:08:43,828
I really blew it.

1093
01:08:48,415 --> 01:08:50,209
This was your Christmas present.

1094
01:08:51,502 --> 01:08:53,170
It's kind of a mess though.

1095
01:09:06,934 --> 01:09:08,811
Did you get hurt?

1096
01:09:11,021 --> 01:09:12,064
What are you doing?

1097
01:09:23,242 --> 01:09:25,077
I love you, Ayane.

1098
01:09:26,203 --> 01:09:27,413
I can't take it.

1099
01:09:27,496 --> 01:09:30,416
I don't wanna watch
as you walk away from me anymore.

1100
01:09:32,459 --> 01:09:34,753
I... I think you're so cute.

1101
01:09:34,837 --> 01:09:36,797
And I love you so much.

1102
01:09:37,756 --> 01:09:40,759
The way you're awkward. And a big softie!

1103
01:09:40,843 --> 01:09:42,011
I love that!

1104
01:09:42,678 --> 01:09:43,554
I love you!

1105
01:09:45,014 --> 01:09:47,683
If you've never been in love
with anyone before,

1106
01:09:47,766 --> 01:09:49,310
then fall in love with me!

1107
01:09:50,019 --> 01:09:51,937
Even if it's not all at once.

1108
01:09:52,897 --> 01:09:54,982
Just fall in love with me, okay?

1109
01:09:56,358 --> 01:09:57,610
I'll cherish you.

1110
01:09:58,694 --> 01:10:01,030
I'll treasure you so much, Ayane!

1111
01:10:21,050 --> 01:10:22,134
Okay.
